abstract: >-
  OpenGenesis-BioCore is a local-first, extensible bioinformatics platform
  designed for reproducible analysis workflows on Windows and Linux. Version
  0.3.0 adds a canonical small-variant model, VCF ingestion and normalization,
  local indel candidate realignment, unified probabilistic genotyping, advanced
  filtering, generic prioritization, versioned local reference databases,
  feature-overlap annotation, multi-sample matrices, case/control association,
  indexed variant workspace queries, provenance-preserving export, and
  truth-set benchmarking while retaining the C++20 native core, localhost
  browser interface, SQLite project persistence, plugins and pipelines.

